{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1538475-multiple-actions-and-grapple","id":1538475,"title":"Multiple actions and grapple","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-12T06:50:01-07:00","id":1538475,"title":"Multiple actions and grapple","content":"I had the case for the first time in my last session, one of my pc and his ennemy has gone on a grapple inititated by the pc. On the next round the pc use celerity to take 2 action against his target, the first was meant to maintain the grappling (which succeeded) and the second was for biting his target.<br /> <br /> Few questions came out from this event:<br /> <br /> -When you are grappled, can you take 2 actions to free yourself? And in that case does your opponent have to take 2 actions to keep you grappled?<br /> <br /> -If you're the grappler taking 2 actions, do you benefit from the difficulty reduction against immobilized enemies on your second action against him?<br /> <br /> -In the case of a pc gone in frenzy, how do you solve it if his 2 or 3 friends use grappling to keep him still? Does he must roll once for each grappler? Does the strongest roll for everyone, with 1 bonus die for each participant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T16:28:04-07:00","id":1538497,"title":"","content":"The books are... frustratingly unclear about this and each edition with each different game line have their own odd wrinkles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T16:47:55-07:00","id":1538500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1538475-multiple-actions-and-grapple?p=1538497#post1538497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The books are... frustratingly unclear about this and each edition with each different game line have their own odd wrinkles.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what i thought... any advice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T17:44:14-07:00","id":1538501,"title":"","content":"I'd go with only allowing one attempt at escape per combat turn to cut down on the potential for adding weird meta to grappling actions. Sufficiently strong and heavy characters might be able to use multiple action powers to move while dragging the would-be grappler around, like if most vampires attempt to &quot;subdue&quot; a Garou in Crinos (and wrestling with a kaiju-sized character's big toe probably isn't a productive use of time or effort).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T18:32:07-07:00","id":1538504,"title":"","content":"So, IME, grappling in most readings of the rules is a positive for characters with less actions, and this is a good thing. Considering how much Celerty/Rage/etc. can make fights extremely lopsided, having some relatively simple strategy to put them in check makes for better play experiences.<br /> <br /> To that, I generally handle the questions in the following fashion:<br /> <br /> 1) The person in control of the grapple rolls once per turn to maintain the grapple. Multiple actions allow multiple rolls to escape, but you have to beat the same target each time. If you get grabbed by Strength 5/Potence 5 (with bp for autosuccesses)/Brawl 5 vampire, and you don't have superstrength? Multiple actions is either a hail mary in hopes you get an insanely fluke roll, or a waist of energy. That threat should be real, and force &quot;speedster&quot; characters to be tactical and think about how to use their multiple actions effectively instead of just overwhelming targets with action economy.<br /> <br /> 2) Yes, if a grappler is in control of a grapple and takes multiple action, they can use one to immobilize and the other to do damage. IME it's generally something that either makes a one-sided fight go faster, or is a choice with risks to make multiple grappling actions (since splitting your pool or spending points for actions isn't free). It's also pretty much the only way for certain moves in some of the books (particularly WtA ones) to work.<br /> <br /> 3) Each grappler has to be escaped individually. If three people are dog-piling on one person and they're all of roughly equal ability, that's not something you should be able to just toss off with ease. You might get loose from one, but that one will grab you again while you're trying to get the others off of you. If you out-skill or overpower your opponents,then it's more sensible you can get out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T09:42:59-07:00","id":1538521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1538475-multiple-actions-and-grapple?p=1538504#post1538504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) The person in control of the grapple rolls once per turn to maintain the grapple. Multiple actions allow multiple rolls to escape, but you have to beat the same target each time. If you get grabbed by Strength 5/Potence 5 (with bp for autosuccesses)/Brawl 5 vampire, and you don't have superstrength? Multiple actions is either a hail mary in hopes you get an insanely fluke roll, or a waist of energy. That threat should be real, and force &quot;speedster&quot; characters to be tactical and think about how to use their multiple actions effectively instead of just overwhelming targets with action economy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure i understant this one, are you saying the grappler roll only one time to maintain the grapple and the grappled just get multiple try to get more success to free himself?<br /> <br /> Exemple: John catch Harry, John get 6 success to maintain his grip, Harry take 3 action to break free and get 2 success the first try, 5 on the second and 3 the third. None of his 3 rolls allowed him to surpass John's success so he stay grappled. On the other hand he could have use his additionnal success to attack John and free himself by killing him or make him want to let go to protect himself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 07-26-2024, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T14:31:00-07:00","id":1538543,"title":"","content":"In most versions of the WoD combat system, the subject of the grapple can't damage the grappler unless they win control of the grapple. Otherwise yes. Harry's three tries fail to get him out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T03:17:20-07:00","id":1539919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1538475-multiple-actions-and-grapple?p=1538543#post1538543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In most versions of the WoD combat system, the subject of the grapple can't damage the grappler unless they win control of the grapple.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the case where the subject of the grapple try to bite, or dig his claws in the limbs holding him back? All he have to do is move his finger for the claws and we saw in some movie a character biting their ennemy to get free.<br /> <br /> With a multiple action and a roll at higher difficulty (8 for exemple) even if it doesn't deal any damage the pain could help him getting free easier. It could use Dex or Wits + subterfuge or simply allowing him to roll 1 to 3 more dice on his try to beat the grapple success","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T17:20:24-07:00","id":1539961,"title":"","content":"That's just a way to describe winning control of the grapple and then possibly doing damage with that control... as far as the rules are written. The WoD combat rules aren't exactly a highlight of the system, and grappling even less so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}